    "updated_at": "2024-10-29T15:26:09Z",
    "body": "> The way the same integer seed is passed around in the [chemistry tutorial](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-sqd/tutorials/01_chemistry_hamiltonian.html#Iteratively-refine-the-samples-using-configuration-recovery-and-approximate-the-ground-state-at-each-iteration) might be statistically invalid. Again, a single Generator instance should be created and passed instead.\n\n@kevinsung , I don't quite understand why a single seed, used in different contexts, would cause some degeneracy. All it does is fix the randomness for each of these functions to make things deterministic. If the seed is causing some anomalous behavior, you can just change it and make sure that behavior stops.\n\nCould you please explain what you mean here?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
