    "created_at": "2024-10-29T16:02:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-29T16:02:47Z",
    "body": "An integer seed is used to set the internal state of a pseudo-random number generator (PRNG). If the same seed is used at two different points in time, then the PRNG will have the same internal state at those different points in time, and its results won't be statistically independent.\n\n>All it does is fix the randomness for each of these functions to make things deterministic.\n\nThe performance of SQD relies on the random numbers drawn at different points of time being statistically independent. While seeding is needed to make results deterministic, care needs to be taken when seeding to ensure that the results are statistically valid.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
